ing of the Java  *)\n(* class.                                                                  *)\n(***************************************************************************)\nEXTENDS Naturals\n\nInt  ==  { }\n(***************************************************************************)\n(* This defines the prefix - operator.                                     *)\n(***************************************************************************)\n-. a == 0 - a\n=============================================================================\n", display: "<standard>/Integers.tla", module: "Integers", standard: true }, FileInfo { source: "-------------------------------- MODULE Naturals ----------------------------\n(***************************************************************************)\n(* This module provides dummy definitions of the operators that are        *)\n(* defined by the real Naturals module.  It is expected that any tool will *)\n(* provide its own implementations of these operators.  See the book       *)\n(* \"Specifying Systems\" for the real Naturals module.                      *)\n(***************************************************************************)\n(***************************************************************************)\n(* These definitions are all overridden by TLC in the Java class           *)\n(* tlc2.module.Naturals. Each operator is overridden by the Java method    *)\n(* with the same name, except that the mapping for TLA+ infix operators    *)\n(* is defined in the static block at the beginning of the Java class.      *)\n(***************************************************************************)\nNat       == { }\na+b       == {a, b}\n\na-b       == CHOOSE n : b + n = a\na*b       == TRUE\na^b       == {a, b}\na<b       ==  a = b\na>b       ==  a = b\na \\leq b  ==  a = b\na \\geq b  ==  a = b\n(***************************************************************************)\n(* a .. b  is defined to equal  {i \\in Int : (a \\leq i) /\\ (i \\leq b)}     *)\n(* where  Int  is the set of all integers.                                 *)\n(*                                                                         *)\n(* a % b  and  a \\div b  are defined so that for any integers  a  and  b   *)\n(* with  b > 0 , the following formula is true:                            *)\n(*                                                                         *)\n(*    a  =  b * (a \\div b) + (a % b)                                       *)\n(***************************************************************************)\na % b     ==  {a, b}\na \\div b  ==  {a, b}\na .. b    ==  {a, b}\n=============================================================================\n", display: "<standard>/Naturals.tla", module: "Naturals", standard: true }], modules: [Module { name: "Naturals", file: Some(FileId(2)), nesting: 0, parent: None, standard: true, instantiated: false, extends: [], context: [("Nat", Def(DefId(0))), ("+", Def(DefId(1))), ("-", Def(DefId(2))), ("*", Def(DefId(3))), ("^", Def(DefId(4))), ("<", Def(DefId(5))), (">", Def(DefId(6))), ("\\leq", Def(DefId(7))), ("\\geq", Def(DefId(8))), ("%", Def(DefId(9))), ("\\div", Def(DefId(10))), ("..", Def(DefId(11)))], assumptions: [], theorems: [], axioms: [], tlc_constants: [] }, Module { name: "Integers", file: Some(FileId(1)), nesting: 0, parent: None, standard: true, instantiated: false, extends: [ModuleId(0)], context: [("Nat", Def(DefId(0))), ("+", Def(DefId(1))), ("-", Def(DefId(2))), ("*", Def(DefId(3))), ("^", Def(DefId(4))), ("<", Def(DefId(5))), (">", Def(DefId(6))), ("\\leq", Def(DefId(7))), ("\\geq", Def(DefId(8))), ("%", Def(DefId(9))), ("\\div", Def(DefId(10))), ("..", Def(DefId(11))), ("Int", Def(DefId(12))), ("-.", Def(DefId(13)))], assumptions: [], theorems: [], axioms: [], tlc_constants: [] }, Module { name: "TiLet", file: Some(FileId(0)), nesting: 0, parent: None, standard: false, instantiated: false, extends: [ModuleId(1)], context: [("Nat", 